WEBVTT

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.925
Welcome to the E D C S complete user training.

00:00:04.045 --> 00:00:10.365
We will work through administration and every operational module using fictional training records.

00:00:10.485 --> 00:00:13.800
Follow the chapter list to revisit a topic.

00:00:13.920 --> 00:00:18.715
Your actual menu depends on your account permissions and assigned districts.

00:00:19.765 --> 00:00:26.885
Enter the username and password supplied by your administrator, then choose Sign in to your workspace.

00:00:27.005 --> 00:00:29.025
Passwords stay masked.

00:00:29.145 --> 00:00:31.955
An inactive account cannot sign in.

00:00:32.075 --> 00:00:36.770
If you need access or a password reset, contact your administrator.

00:00:36.890 --> 00:00:39.765
Do not share another officer’s account.

00:00:40.815 --> 00:00:44.060
An administrator lands in the control center.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:47.465
Ordinary users land in their workspace.

00:00:47.585 --> 00:00:51.755
Use the left navigation to move between permitted modules.

00:00:51.875 --> 00:00:56.580
The controls shown here are available because this is a training administrator.

00:00:56.700 --> 00:01:00.405
We will also demonstrate a restricted user later.

00:01:01.455 --> 00:01:11.160
Overview summarizes the members you are authorized to see, including recent registrations, admission trends, active members and location counts.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.520
Ordinary users see only their assigned districts.

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:20.005
The overview is a summary; open a module to enter or review its detailed records.

00:01:21.055 --> 00:01:24.680
Open Administration, then Roles and permissions.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:28.595
Roles are reusable collections of module actions.

00:01:28.715 --> 00:01:31.755
View, Add, Edit and Delete are independent.

00:01:31.875 --> 00:01:40.210
Giving someone View does not let them change records, and staff status alone does not grant workspace administration.

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:43.450
Give the role a clear name.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:47.415
In the Members row, select View and Add for this example.

00:01:47.535 --> 00:01:50.105
Leave Edit and Delete unselected.

00:01:50.225 --> 00:01:53.345
Review the other module rows before saving.

00:01:53.465 --> 00:02:00.785
Permissions from all roles and direct grants are combined, so removing one grant may not remove effective access.

00:02:01.835 --> 00:02:03.285
Save the role.

00:02:03.405 --> 00:02:06.795
It is now available when creating or editing a user.

00:02:06.915 --> 00:02:13.985
A role controls actions, while district assignments control which district records those actions can affect.

00:02:14.105 --> 00:02:17.440
A role never expands the user’s district list.

00:02:18.490 --> 00:02:23.385
Open Users and access to search accounts and review whether they are active.

00:02:23.505 --> 00:02:27.420
Choose an existing username to edit it or create a new user.

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:34.815
Administrators can reset passwords, assign roles, select districts and set direct module permissions.

00:02:35.865 --> 00:02:44.805
Enter a unique username, the employee’s name and, when applicable, a unique E P F number and ledger officer zonal office.

00:02:44.925 --> 00:02:47.855
Set and confirm a strong initial password.

00:02:47.975 --> 00:02:49.885
Email is optional.

00:02:50.005 --> 00:02:56.195
If supplied, the welcome message contains the username and sign-in link, not the password.

00:02:57.245 --> 00:03:01.975
Assign the registration role and select Colombo for this example.

00:03:02.095 --> 00:03:07.175
An ordinary user with no districts cannot access district records.

00:03:07.295 --> 00:03:11.800
Selecting a district does not grant module actions by itself.

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:18.985
A ledger officer must be active, have an E P F number and match the responsible zonal office and district.

00:03:20.035 --> 00:03:23.540
Review the direct-permission matrix as well as roles.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:26.180
Grant only the required actions.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:30.005
Save user and access applies the account changes.

00:03:30.125 --> 00:03:38.255
On existing accounts, leave password fields blank to keep the password, or enter both new password fields to reset it.

00:03:39.305 --> 00:03:40.995
The account is saved.

00:03:41.115 --> 00:03:46.515
Role, district and permission changes take effect on subsequent requests.

00:03:46.635 --> 00:03:51.990
Deactivate an account to stop access, but first reassign its active ledgers.

00:03:52.110 --> 00:03:56.460
Permanent responsibility and approval history can prevent deletion.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:04:00.955
The control center records account and role administration activity.

00:04:02.005 --> 00:04:05.420
This is the registration user we just created.

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:10.335
The directory shows its assigned district, with registration available.

00:04:10.455 --> 00:04:15.805
Edit, deletion, finance and administration are not granted by this role.

00:04:15.925 --> 00:04:22.765
If a menu or action is missing, ask an administrator to check effective permissions and district access.

00:04:23.815 --> 00:04:28.230
Set up organizational masters before registering members.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:29.975
Start with Districts.

00:04:30.095 --> 00:04:33.140
The system includes Sri Lankan districts.

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:39.805
Search the list and open a district to review its code, province information and linked records.

00:04:39.925 --> 00:04:43.380
Only administrators can create new districts.

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:48.720
A district stores its full province name and a separate short name.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:53.835
Here Colombo belongs to Western, with W P as its abbreviation.

00:04:53.955 --> 00:04:57.755
The member form derives these values from the selected district.

00:04:57.875 --> 00:05:01.775
Do not replace the full province name with an abbreviation.

00:05:02.825 --> 00:05:05.855
Save approved corrections and verify the list.

00:05:05.975 --> 00:05:12.475
Master records with linked operational data are protected from unsafe deletion or parent changes.

00:05:12.595 --> 00:05:17.670
Where supported, mark a master inactive instead of deleting its history.

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:21.720
Inactive choices are not normally offered for new assignments.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:25.310
Zonal offices belong to districts.

00:05:25.430 --> 00:05:32.180
Open Zonal offices to search or filter the list and follow links to their departments, lagers and members.

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:37.990
Review the existing master before adding another office so the same office is not entered twice.

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:45.745
Choose the district, enter the office name and code, and provide the office contact details if available.

00:05:45.865 --> 00:05:49.635
Keep Active selected when it should be available for new work.

00:05:49.755 --> 00:05:54.990
The member’s own office address and phone are entered separately during registration.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.360
Save and check the office in the list.

00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:03.555
An office used by related records cannot be moved to a conflicting district.

00:06:03.675 --> 00:06:10.890
Assign eligible ledger officers to the correct zone before using that zone for registration or transfers.

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:16.710
Subdivisions are optional organizational units within a zonal office.

00:06:16.830 --> 00:06:21.690
Use the master list to maintain them when the business structure needs them.

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:27.575
A member may leave subdivision blank, even when the department has an associated subdivision.

00:06:28.625 --> 00:06:34.515
Select the district and one of its zonal offices, then enter a clear subdivision name and code.

00:06:34.635 --> 00:06:37.700
The subdivision must belong to the selected zone.

00:06:37.820 --> 00:06:43.825
Save only after checking the relationship; a location mismatch is rejected by the server.

00:06:44.875 --> 00:06:49.895
The saved subdivision can now appear in compatible department and member forms.

00:06:50.015 --> 00:06:54.310
Keep linked history intact when making later master changes.

00:06:54.430 --> 00:07:01.530
Deactivating an old subdivision is different from moving existing members to a new organizational location.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:07.880
Departments connect a district and zonal office, with an optional subdivision.

00:07:08.000 --> 00:07:11.675
Search by name or code and use district filters.

00:07:11.795 --> 00:07:19.020
Department selection is required during member registration and helps fill the correct location information.

00:07:20.070 --> 00:07:24.600
Choose the district and zone, then select a matching subdivision if needed.

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:27.310
Enter the department code and name.

00:07:27.430 --> 00:07:30.165
The province fields come from the district.

00:07:30.285 --> 00:07:36.095
The full department label helps distinguish departments with similar names in different locations.

00:07:37.145 --> 00:07:41.560
After saving, the department is available to eligible users.

00:07:41.680 --> 00:07:49.230
A registered member’s zone or department change must use Member Transfers so the original ledger is preserved.

00:07:49.350 --> 00:07:54.650
Do not edit a master or bypass a location guard simply to move registered members.

00:07:55.700 --> 00:07:59.290
A lager is a named member group under a zonal office.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:03.555
Filter by district and zone, or search by name or code.

00:08:03.675 --> 00:08:09.505
The list shows member counts and links to the lager’s members and consolidated activity.

00:08:10.555 --> 00:08:16.020
Select the district and zonal office, then enter a name and globally unique code.

00:08:16.140 --> 00:08:21.170
The same lager name may exist in different zones, but not twice in the same zone.

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:25.670
Registration requires a lager from the department’s zonal office.

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:28.970
Save and verify the result.

00:08:29.090 --> 00:08:34.360
A lager containing members cannot simply move to another zone or be deleted.

00:08:34.480 --> 00:08:38.920
Use the supported member location workflows and retain history.

00:08:39.040 --> 00:08:43.050
We will return to Lager activity in the reporting chapter.

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:47.710
Open Member directory and choose Register member.

00:08:47.830 --> 00:08:50.715
Required fields are marked on the form.

00:08:50.835 --> 00:08:54.415
Begin with the department or location selectors.

00:08:54.535 --> 00:09:02.370
You may search a department by name or code; its saved relationships fill district, zone and province information.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:07.310
Select a compatible lager and the ledger maintenance officer.

00:09:07.430 --> 00:09:13.200
The officer must be active with an E P F number and the correct office and district access.

00:09:13.320 --> 00:09:18.390
New registration creates an original ledger with this responsibility.

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:22.075
Changing zone clears incompatible choices.

00:09:23.125 --> 00:09:28.250
Enter the member number, full name and national identity number carefully.

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:33.715
Member number, nonblank computer number and N I C must be unique.

00:09:33.835 --> 00:09:36.760
Choose the optional title and birth date.

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:42.865
Short Name and expected retirement are generated; the retirement age defaults to sixty.

00:09:43.915 --> 00:09:48.995
Complete salary, admission date, mobile number and both addresses.

00:09:49.115 --> 00:09:51.720
Office and home phone are optional.

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:54.935
Office contact details are entered manually.

00:09:55.055 --> 00:10:00.480
Salary cannot be negative, and admission or birth dates cannot be in the future.

00:10:00.600 --> 00:10:02.875
Keep Active for a current member.

00:10:03.925 --> 00:10:07.870
Review all required fields and submit the registration.

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:13.510
The button may continue to payment-plan setup if your account has that separate Add permission.

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:18.690
Registration permission alone does not grant financial module access.

00:10:18.810 --> 00:10:22.100
Correct any field errors before submitting again.

00:10:23.150 --> 00:10:29.855
The profile confirms the saved member, generated short name, location and contacts.

00:10:29.975 --> 00:10:33.175
Its original ledger reference is retained.

00:10:33.295 --> 00:10:41.555
Use the profile’s authorized links for plans, openings, financial entries, children, retirement or transfers.

00:10:41.675 --> 00:10:45.070
Each linked section still needs its own permission.

00:10:46.120 --> 00:10:54.155
Search by member number, name, short name, national identity number, computer number or mobile phone.

00:10:54.275 --> 00:11:00.155
Combine district, zonal office, department, lager and status filters when needed.

00:11:00.275 --> 00:11:03.500
Sorting and pagination help with larger lists.

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:06.975
Only authorized district records are returned.

00:11:08.025 --> 00:11:11.535
Open Edit to correct permitted member details.

00:11:11.655 --> 00:11:14.130
Here we add an optional home phone.

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:16.870
Generated fields remain read-only.

00:11:16.990 --> 00:11:20.745
Zone or department moves use Member Transfers.

00:11:20.865 --> 00:11:27.835
If a matching edit hierarchy is active, saving submits an approval request before changing business data.

00:11:28.885 --> 00:11:34.185
Check the profile’s identity, location and permitted financial summaries.

00:11:34.305 --> 00:11:39.090
Printing is intended for an authorized user who has already checked the record.

00:11:39.210 --> 00:11:43.950
Do not assume printed figures replace a dated financial statement.

00:11:45.000 --> 00:11:53.340
The browser print layout removes workspace navigation and prepares the profile for paper or the browser’s Save as P D F option.

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:57.960
Choose the appropriate printer and protect printed member information.

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:01.675
We are showing the print styling with fictional training data.

00:12:02.725 --> 00:12:07.930
Use Export C S V to download the matching authorized directory records.

00:12:08.050 --> 00:12:14.000
Applied filters determine the exported set, including records beyond the visible page.

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:17.915
Open the file in your approved spreadsheet application.

00:12:18.035 --> 00:12:23.255
The system escapes potentially dangerous spreadsheet formula prefixes.

00:12:24.305 --> 00:12:27.815
An expected retirement date is planning information.

00:12:27.935 --> 00:12:31.280
It does not automatically change the member’s status.

00:12:31.400 --> 00:12:36.985
To record an actual retirement, open the profile and choose Process retirement.

00:12:37.105 --> 00:12:41.905
Early retirement can be recorded using its actual authorized date.

00:12:42.955 --> 00:12:48.270
Choose today or an earlier actual retirement date, after the member’s birth date.

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:52.565
This records the pension date and changes status to Retired.

00:12:52.685 --> 00:12:56.310
The pension-date quarter affects member deposit interest.

00:12:56.430 --> 00:13:01.830
Posted-year protection can reject a change that would rewrite closed eligibility.

00:13:02.880 --> 00:13:09.710
The member is now retired, with financial accounts, payment plans and transaction history retained.

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:14.610
The profile’s recorded pension date is distinct from expected retirement.

00:13:14.730 --> 00:13:20.400
A parent’s pension date does not remove interest from the child’s separate deposit accounts.

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:28.750
Payment Types is the shared master for categories such as Special Deposit, Fix Deposit, Share and Pension.

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:32.000
Scholarship and Scholar are separate types.

00:13:32.120 --> 00:13:37.590
Administrators manage these settings; ordinary users need View to read the master.

00:13:38.640 --> 00:13:44.830
Open a type to review its name, active status, display order and annual interest rate.

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:48.380
Rates range from zero to one hundred percent.

00:13:48.500 --> 00:13:51.045
A zero rate may be intentional.

00:13:51.165 --> 00:13:56.100
Review finance policy before changing a rate used in calculations.

00:13:57.150 --> 00:14:02.665
Custom reference settings can describe a repeating interval or specific start and end dates.

00:14:02.785 --> 00:14:05.625
Here the draft shows forty-five days.

00:14:05.745 --> 00:14:08.555
These settings are reference information.

00:14:08.675 --> 00:14:17.220
The Quarterly Interest module still uses its quarterly minimum month-end calculation; it does not switch to a forty-five-day engine.

00:14:18.270 --> 00:14:21.435
We return to the quarterly reference and save.

00:14:21.555 --> 00:14:26.020
Active new payment types appear in relevant plan and opening forms.

00:14:26.140 --> 00:14:29.505
Inactive types retain historical amounts.

00:14:29.625 --> 00:14:33.865
Used types cannot be deleted just to remove old history.

00:14:34.915 --> 00:14:38.990
Plan templates provide reusable contribution amounts.

00:14:39.110 --> 00:14:43.310
They contain no member balances and are shared across districts.

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:47.960
Template permissions are separate from member payment-plan permissions.

00:14:48.080 --> 00:14:51.940
An existing member plan keeps its own copied amounts.

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:58.680
Enter a name and description, then positive monthly amounts for the relevant payment types.

00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:01.700
Leave unused types blank or zero.

00:15:01.820 --> 00:15:06.090
A usable template needs at least one positive contribution.

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:09.585
Keep Active when operators should be able to apply it.

00:15:10.635 --> 00:15:11.930
Save the template.

00:15:12.050 --> 00:15:18.630
Applying it copies amounts into a member’s draft plan, where an authorized operator can adjust them.

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:23.830
Changing or deleting the template later does not update already assigned plans.

00:15:23.950 --> 00:15:29.355
Do not expect a template revision to alter every member agreement automatically.

00:15:30.405 --> 00:15:34.600
The Payment Plan directory uses saved member identities.

00:15:34.720 --> 00:15:39.310
Search by member number or name and review pending versus ready agreements.

00:15:39.430 --> 00:15:41.700
Each member has one current plan.

00:15:41.820 --> 00:15:46.790
In this example we will set a plan for training member zero zero zero one.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:50.820
Select an active template to load its amounts.

00:15:50.940 --> 00:15:52.725
The form remains a draft.

00:15:52.845 --> 00:15:59.110
Review each payment type, customize the member’s agreed amounts when authorized, and check the total.

00:15:59.230 --> 00:16:03.805
Selecting another template explicitly replaces the draft amounts.

00:16:04.855 --> 00:16:08.335
Enter the agreement date and review the monthly total.

00:16:08.455 --> 00:16:11.965
This is an agreement about expected contributions.

00:16:12.085 --> 00:16:16.010
Saving a plan does not create an actual deposit or a debit.

00:16:16.130 --> 00:16:20.985
Received money must be entered through the appropriate transaction workflow.

00:16:22.035 --> 00:16:25.600
The saved plan shows its agreement and type amounts.

00:16:25.720 --> 00:16:29.065
Open Edit to change it later if you have permission.

00:16:29.185 --> 00:16:35.215
Saved opening balances may be shown only with the separate Opening Balances View permission.

00:16:35.335 --> 00:16:39.050
Deleting an eligible plan keeps the member registered.

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:44.630
Opening Balances stores imported starting amounts by payment type.

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:49.285
Choose a member number or name and check whether a record already exists.

00:16:49.405 --> 00:16:54.490
A member has one opening record, separate from the monthly contribution plan.

00:16:55.540 --> 00:17:00.300
Choose Balance as of and enter each payment type’s starting amount in rupees.

00:17:00.420 --> 00:17:03.290
Unused amounts may be blank or zero.

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:08.040
Here Special Deposit starts at ten thousand and Share at two thousand.

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:11.285
Check the total and source records before saving.

00:17:12.335 --> 00:17:15.860
The saved page separates opening amounts by type.

00:17:15.980 --> 00:17:24.070
Later annual interest carry-forward is shown through its saved results without replacing the original imported opening record.

00:17:24.190 --> 00:17:29.965
Transfers also use ledger snapshots rather than duplicate opening records.

00:17:31.015 --> 00:17:35.160
Existing openings can be edited only when domain rules allow it.

00:17:35.280 --> 00:17:42.880
Posted interest, Fix Deposit loan or withdrawal history, and historical ledgers can lock amounts or dates.

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:49.570
Ask the responsible finance officer to investigate a locked value instead of bypassing the protection.

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:53.440
Open Debit and Credit, then Add entry.

00:17:53.560 --> 00:17:57.405
Select the member, payment type and financial date.

00:17:57.525 --> 00:18:05.390
The saved balance preview includes applicable openings and earlier saved transactions, excluding the unsaved entry.

00:18:05.510 --> 00:18:08.310
Verify the account before entering money.

00:18:09.360 --> 00:18:13.905
For a deposit, enter a positive credit and leave debit blank or zero.

00:18:14.025 --> 00:18:18.965
For an ordinary withdrawal, enter a positive debit and leave credit zero.

00:18:19.085 --> 00:18:21.975
Both positive or both zero are invalid.

00:18:22.095 --> 00:18:27.590
Enter a useful reference and description, then check the saved-balance context.

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:36.025
The statement shows starting or brought-forward balance, period debits and credits, running balances and final balance.

00:18:36.145 --> 00:18:40.610
Final balance equals starting balance plus credits minus debits.

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:46.815
Earlier movements are brought forward when you narrow the period; the account does not reset to zero.

00:18:47.865 --> 00:18:52.335
Choose either Single date or From and To dates, then show the statement.

00:18:52.455 --> 00:18:54.370
Do not mix both modes.

00:18:54.490 --> 00:19:00.780
The displayed totals apply to the selected period and running balances remain consistent across pages.

00:19:00.900 --> 00:19:04.245
Accounts can be negative where product rules permit.

00:19:05.295 --> 00:19:10.440
Member balances aggregates authorized members and payment types for the selected date.

00:19:10.560 --> 00:19:12.890
Filters can narrow the report.

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:16.890
Its totals cover matching records beyond a single page.

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:20.495
Use View statement to inspect a member and type.

00:19:20.615 --> 00:19:25.875
Fix Deposit withdrawals use their controlled module rather than a generic debit.

00:19:26.925 --> 00:19:30.625
Child Deposit Types is a separate shared master.

00:19:30.745 --> 00:19:36.220
It stores the age at which the rate changes and annual rates below and from that age.

00:19:36.340 --> 00:19:40.830
Member payment types and child deposit types are different masters.

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:49.325
This training type uses age eighteen, eight percent below the threshold and five percent from the threshold birthday.

00:19:49.445 --> 00:19:54.055
Administrators can configure these values within the allowed ranges.

00:19:54.175 --> 00:19:59.835
Review policy before saving because the rule affects current rate displays and new entries.

00:20:00.885 --> 00:20:05.180
Saved child entry rates are retained when the master changes.

00:20:05.300 --> 00:20:09.445
Posted annual calculation snapshots also stay fixed.

00:20:09.565 --> 00:20:18.395
The threshold-birthday quarter is excluded from quarterly interest; it is not prorated, even when the two configured rates happen to be equal.

00:20:19.445 --> 00:20:23.380
Open Children from the workspace or a member profile.

00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:25.865
A member may have several children.

00:20:25.985 --> 00:20:34.810
Children permissions are separate from Child Deposits permissions, so seeing a child does not automatically reveal that child’s savings.

00:20:35.860 --> 00:20:42.260
Confirm the parent member, enter the child’s name and date of birth, and keep Active if appropriate.

00:20:42.380 --> 00:20:44.880
Birth date cannot be in the future.

00:20:45.000 --> 00:20:51.100
After saving, the parent relationship remains fixed to protect account and family history.

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:55.965
The child profile shows saved identity and age.

00:20:56.085 --> 00:21:01.290
Authorized users can open deposit accounts or follow existing account links.

00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:06.835
A child may have more than one deposit, including more than one account of the same type.

00:21:06.955 --> 00:21:10.100
Keep the account reference clear when posting.

00:21:11.150 --> 00:21:18.230
Child Deposits lists accounts with their own references, balances and configured age-based rates as of a date.

00:21:18.350 --> 00:21:21.585
Filter by parent member, child or type.

00:21:21.705 --> 00:21:26.270
These balances never merge with the parent’s separate member payment account.

00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:31.275
Choose the child deposit type, opening date and amount.

00:21:31.395 --> 00:21:35.500
The rate preview follows the child’s completed age on that date.

00:21:35.620 --> 00:21:42.310
The opening date cannot be before birth or in the future, and the opening amount cannot be negative.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:46.310
Save and note the generated deposit reference.

00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:55.275
Multiple accounts of one type can exist for the same child, so name and type alone are not enough to identify a posting destination.

00:21:55.395 --> 00:22:01.625
Opening amount and date become fixed once dated transactions or posted annual interest exist.

00:22:02.675 --> 00:22:06.155
Open the intended deposit and choose Add debit or credit.

00:22:06.275 --> 00:22:09.510
Enter the date and exactly one positive side.

00:22:09.630 --> 00:22:12.855
Here we credit seven hundred and fifty rupees.

00:22:12.975 --> 00:22:17.835
Verify the account reference, saved balance and configured rate before saving.

00:22:17.955 --> 00:22:20.890
An entry cannot predate account opening.

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:28.635
The child statement shows opening or brought-forward amount, movements and running balance for this account only.

00:22:28.755 --> 00:22:31.995
Apply a single date or inclusive range as needed.

00:22:32.115 --> 00:22:38.475
Its final balance uses the opening amount plus saved credits minus debits through the chosen date.

00:22:39.525 --> 00:22:43.110
An entry stores the applicable configured rate when saved.

00:22:43.230 --> 00:22:45.980
Changing a note or amount keeps that rate.

00:22:46.100 --> 00:22:51.160
An allowed transaction-date change in an open year refreshes it under current rules.

00:22:51.280 --> 00:22:55.990
Closed years and historical ledgers may prevent editing or deletion.

00:22:57.040 --> 00:23:01.175
Open Quarterly Interest and choose the financial year and account group.

00:23:01.295 --> 00:23:07.985
You can include member accounts, child deposits or both, then narrow by the available filters.

00:23:08.105 --> 00:23:10.780
Viewing a preview does not credit interest.

00:23:10.900 --> 00:23:14.425
This example reviews the ended twenty twenty-five year.

00:23:15.475 --> 00:23:20.080
Each completed quarter uses the minimum of its three month-end balances.

00:23:20.200 --> 00:23:26.705
Quarterly interest is that minimum times the annual percentage divided by four hundred, rounded to cents.

00:23:26.825 --> 00:23:31.845
A nonpositive minimum earns zero, and an incomplete quarter remains pending.

00:23:32.895 --> 00:23:37.005
The member’s pension-date quarter is excluded from member interest.

00:23:37.125 --> 00:23:42.475
A child’s age-threshold birthday quarter is excluded only for that child account.

00:23:42.595 --> 00:23:46.180
Parent retirement does not exclude child savings.

00:23:46.300 --> 00:23:51.235
Confirm rates and dates before closing because posted history is protected.

00:23:52.285 --> 00:23:56.825
Review year-end posting only after the saved financial year has ended.

00:23:56.945 --> 00:24:01.480
Check quarter results, annual interest and next opening amount.

00:24:01.600 --> 00:24:06.895
The system rejects a stale review if underlying calculation inputs change.

00:24:07.015 --> 00:24:11.935
With an active matching hierarchy, the posting request waits for approval.

00:24:12.985 --> 00:24:17.340
Annual interest is credited once, dated at the financial year end.

00:24:17.460 --> 00:24:20.465
It is not capitalized every quarter.

00:24:20.585 --> 00:24:27.045
The result becomes part of next year’s brought-forward balance while the original opening and entries remain.

00:24:27.165 --> 00:24:30.750
Repeating a supported post does not create another credit.

00:24:31.800 --> 00:24:38.600
Child annual interest has its own review and posts to the child’s deposit, not the parent’s member ledger.

00:24:38.720 --> 00:24:41.665
Check the child and unique account reference.

00:24:41.785 --> 00:24:50.930
After posting, affected historical identity, opening and transaction inputs are protected from changes that rewrite the closed year.

00:24:51.980 --> 00:24:58.620
The system also provides an optional scheduled processor for saving calculations and posting ended years.

00:24:58.740 --> 00:25:04.230
Its installation and posting authority are administrator responsibilities.

00:25:04.350 --> 00:25:12.975
Users should review the configured operating policy and reported failures; do not assume every deployment has the scheduler installed.

00:25:14.025 --> 00:25:19.765
Fix Deposit Loans and Withdrawals uses a policy linked to a member payment type.

00:25:19.885 --> 00:25:26.920
The underlying deposit balance comes from openings, top-up credits and controlled released withdrawals.

00:25:27.040 --> 00:25:30.710
A monthly plan amount by itself is not collateral.

00:25:31.760 --> 00:25:42.960
The training policy uses a thirty-six-month withdrawal cycle, a maximum seventy-five percent withdrawal, ninety percent loan security and twelve months between loan issues.

00:25:43.080 --> 00:25:47.190
A positive loan interest rate is required before issuing a loan.

00:25:47.310 --> 00:25:51.435
These product limits are enforced, not just displayed.

00:25:52.485 --> 00:26:00.655
When creating a Fix Deposit account, select its member and policy and enter the actual start of its withdrawal cycle.

00:26:00.775 --> 00:26:04.495
The cycle may predate a recently imported opening balance.

00:26:04.615 --> 00:26:08.250
There can be only one account for a member and policy.

00:26:08.370 --> 00:26:10.490
Do not guess the cycle date.

00:26:11.540 --> 00:26:16.435
Save the account and confirm its member, policy and cycle start.

00:26:16.555 --> 00:26:20.960
The balance still comes from that member’s existing payment-type ledger.

00:26:21.080 --> 00:26:24.490
Creating an account does not create a new deposit.

00:26:24.610 --> 00:26:29.885
We will use the separate mature training account for the loan and withdrawal examples.

00:26:30.935 --> 00:26:34.225
Our preconfigured fictional account is mature.

00:26:34.345 --> 00:26:44.235
Its status shows deposit balance, outstanding principal and assessed interest, loan capacity, next loan date and withdrawal eligibility.

00:26:44.355 --> 00:26:47.065
Read the reasons when an action is blocked.

00:26:47.185 --> 00:26:50.730
Amounts are calculated for the selected business date.

00:26:51.780 --> 00:26:58.290
Choose Issue loan, check the date, current capacity and configured rate, and enter the principal.

00:26:58.410 --> 00:27:01.135
Here we issue twenty thousand rupees.

00:27:01.255 --> 00:27:05.495
Other outstanding loan principal uses the same collateral limit.

00:27:05.615 --> 00:27:09.280
Issuing this loan does not reduce the deposit balance.

00:27:10.330 --> 00:27:16.605
The loan page keeps its reference, issued principal, issue-date balance and rate snapshot.

00:27:16.725 --> 00:27:19.640
Principal due and assessed interest due are separate.

00:27:19.760 --> 00:27:27.605
A displayed annual rate is not an automatic daily accrual calculation; the bank assesses charges and records them separately.

00:27:28.655 --> 00:27:33.460
Choose an interest charge and enter the assessed amount with zero principal.

00:27:33.580 --> 00:27:40.010
Two hundred rupees is an illustrative training assessment, not a calculation of the displayed annual rate.

00:27:40.130 --> 00:27:44.250
Add a clear reference so the source of the assessment can be checked.

00:27:45.300 --> 00:27:50.530
Choose repayment and enter the principal and assessed-interest amounts being paid.

00:27:50.650 --> 00:27:53.485
Neither may exceed the remaining amount due.

00:27:53.605 --> 00:27:57.850
Here we repay twenty thousand principal and two hundred interest.

00:27:57.970 --> 00:28:03.480
The operation token helps prevent duplicate application of the same submitted repayment.

00:28:04.530 --> 00:28:08.565
A zero displayed balance does not automatically settle the loan.

00:28:08.685 --> 00:28:14.380
Confirm that all interest through settlement has been assessed and paid, then submit settlement.

00:28:14.500 --> 00:28:18.995
The system requires both principal and assessed interest to be zero.

00:28:19.115 --> 00:28:22.955
Configured edit approvals can apply to this processing step.

00:28:24.005 --> 00:28:26.660
The saved loan now records settlement.

00:28:26.780 --> 00:28:34.580
Until all Fix Deposit loans are formally settled, including interest confirmation, withdrawal remains blocked.

00:28:34.700 --> 00:28:41.580
Keep assessment and repayment evidence; do not use generic deposit entries to erase a loan obligation.

00:28:42.630 --> 00:28:44.910
Return to the deposit account.

00:28:45.030 --> 00:28:52.570
Withdrawal requires a mature cycle, no unsettled loans and a positive available amount within the percentage cap.

00:28:52.690 --> 00:28:55.775
Monthly top-ups share the account’s cycle.

00:28:55.895 --> 00:28:59.300
The balance and limits must be checked again at release.

00:29:00.350 --> 00:29:03.360
Enter the request date and permitted amount.

00:29:03.480 --> 00:29:07.190
This example requests twenty-five thousand rupees.

00:29:07.310 --> 00:29:10.530
Creating a request does not debit the deposit.

00:29:10.650 --> 00:29:14.300
Only one pending request can exist for the account.

00:29:14.420 --> 00:29:17.460
Save it for the authorized review process.

00:29:18.510 --> 00:29:23.200
The reviewer chooses release or rejection and confirms the review date.

00:29:23.320 --> 00:29:28.735
Release rechecks maturity, current balance, unsettled loans and the limit.

00:29:28.855 --> 00:29:33.810
Where a matching hierarchy exists, this review waits for final approval.

00:29:33.930 --> 00:29:37.625
Rejection leaves funds and the cycle unchanged.

00:29:38.675 --> 00:29:44.595
Successful release creates one controlled deposit debit and stores before-and-after values.

00:29:44.715 --> 00:29:47.515
The cycle restarts from the release date.

00:29:47.635 --> 00:29:50.960
A repeated review cannot release the request twice.

00:29:51.080 --> 00:29:57.290
Released withdrawal entries cannot be casually edited through the ordinary Debit and Credit screen.

00:29:58.340 --> 00:30:06.085
Member Ledgers shows original and receiving references, active or historical status and responsible officers.

00:30:06.205 --> 00:30:08.675
Use filters to find a page.

00:30:08.795 --> 00:30:16.830
Ledger View does not automatically grant every financial section; those still need their respective module View permissions.

00:30:17.880 --> 00:30:26.235
The ledger retains member and location snapshots, permitted balances, saved record events and responsibility history.

00:30:26.355 --> 00:30:30.155
Financial date and recorded time serve different purposes.

00:30:30.275 --> 00:30:37.070
These pages preserve office continuity; they do not create duplicate transactions from carried amounts.

00:30:38.120 --> 00:30:44.875
Choose Change officer on an active ledger, select an eligible officer from the same zone and record the reason.

00:30:44.995 --> 00:30:49.960
In this example Anita is active with a matching E P F, zone and district.

00:30:50.080 --> 00:30:53.700
Historical ledger pages cannot be reassigned.

00:30:54.750 --> 00:31:01.865
The handover keeps previous and new names and E P F snapshots, the acting user, reason and time.

00:31:01.985 --> 00:31:07.175
Later account-name corrections do not rewrite old responsibility history.

00:31:07.295 --> 00:31:13.935
Reassign active ledgers before deactivating or moving an officer or removing required district access.

00:31:14.985 --> 00:31:22.655
Use Member Transfers when a registered member changes zone or department, including supported changes within a zone.

00:31:22.775 --> 00:31:27.585
The operator needs the transfer action and both source and receiving districts.

00:31:27.705 --> 00:31:31.865
Direct profile changes cannot replace this workflow.

00:31:32.915 --> 00:31:36.475
Select the member and review the current ledger and officer.

00:31:36.595 --> 00:31:41.490
A missing original officer assignment must be resolved before transfer.

00:31:41.610 --> 00:31:48.555
The source reference protects against a stale form if someone transfers the member while your form is open.

00:31:49.605 --> 00:31:56.880
Select the receiving district, zonal office, department, lager, optional matching subdivision and officer.

00:31:57.000 --> 00:31:59.750
Enter a valid effective date and reason.

00:31:59.870 --> 00:32:04.990
Future dates and dates conflicting with later source activity are rejected.

00:32:05.110 --> 00:32:08.255
The receiving officer must be eligible for that office.

00:32:09.305 --> 00:32:14.775
This example has no active transfer hierarchy, so it completes immediately.

00:32:14.895 --> 00:32:20.755
With a configured transfer hierarchy, submission first creates an approval request.

00:32:20.875 --> 00:32:30.005
Successful completion closes and freezes the source page, creates the linked receiving active page and records responsibility atomically.

00:32:31.055 --> 00:32:37.420
Member, child, account, loan, plan and transaction identities remain intact.

00:32:37.540 --> 00:32:40.825
New postings belong to the receiving page.

00:32:40.945 --> 00:32:51.930
The source district retains its historical page without seeing later receiving transactions; receiving users can follow predecessors subject to their section permissions.

00:32:52.980 --> 00:32:57.000
Approval hierarchies are configured by administrators.

00:32:57.120 --> 00:33:02.735
They apply to Member Transfers and edits or processing of existing workspace records.

00:33:02.855 --> 00:33:10.035
Most ordinary creates and deletes, including new loan and repayment entries, follow normal processing.

00:33:10.155 --> 00:33:14.510
Do not assume a global edit hierarchy covers every action.

00:33:15.560 --> 00:33:18.285
Choose the module and supported action.

00:33:18.405 --> 00:33:22.150
This example covers editing member debit and credit entries.

00:33:22.270 --> 00:33:28.495
A module-specific hierarchy takes priority over the global edits-only hierarchy.

00:33:28.615 --> 00:33:35.475
Enter a meaningful configuration reason because the before-and-after settings and approver identities are audited.

00:33:36.525 --> 00:33:41.405
Give each level a distinct order and name, then select its active approvers.

00:33:41.525 --> 00:33:45.085
Any one designated user completes a level.

00:33:45.205 --> 00:33:50.020
Here Supervisor review comes first, then Finance final review.

00:33:50.140 --> 00:33:53.905
Choose whether assigned users may reject at each level.

00:33:54.025 --> 00:33:56.805
Up to twenty levels are supported.

00:33:57.855 --> 00:34:01.215
Review every level and save the hierarchy.

00:34:01.335 --> 00:34:04.545
Ordinary users cannot approve their own requests.

00:34:04.665 --> 00:34:07.715
Administrators can override with a reason.

00:34:07.835 --> 00:34:16.875
Later hierarchy edits do not rewrite the assignments already captured on pending requests; inactive approvers lose access immediately.

00:34:17.925 --> 00:34:20.555
The saved hierarchy appears in the list.

00:34:20.675 --> 00:34:24.790
Its history preserves configuration changes and reasons.

00:34:24.910 --> 00:34:31.855
Deactivating it affects new submissions, while pending requests retain their submitted policy snapshot.

00:34:31.975 --> 00:34:37.050
Use controlled administrator action to resolve affected pending cases.

00:34:38.100 --> 00:34:45.635
As the ordinary operator, edit the saved current-year contribution and request a credit of twenty-six hundred rupees.

00:34:45.755 --> 00:34:49.160
Account identity and original author remain fixed.

00:34:49.280 --> 00:34:55.685
Because the matching hierarchy is active, saving queues the request before changing the transaction.

00:34:56.735 --> 00:35:02.625
The request page shows the submitted change, requester, ordered levels and audit events.

00:35:02.745 --> 00:35:06.520
The transaction still has its earlier amount while pending.

00:35:06.640 --> 00:35:11.680
Requesters see their submissions; designated users see assigned requests.

00:35:11.800 --> 00:35:15.600
A requester can cancel a pending request with a reason.

00:35:16.650 --> 00:35:22.265
The first approver reviews the before-and-after information and decides the current level.

00:35:22.385 --> 00:35:27.810
Another ordinary user cannot skip ahead or approve the requester’s own submission.

00:35:27.930 --> 00:35:31.795
Rejection is available only when enabled for the level.

00:35:31.915 --> 00:35:35.955
Review the actual change rather than approving just its title.

00:35:37.005 --> 00:35:41.195
The first approval advances the request to Finance final review.

00:35:41.315 --> 00:35:44.680
It does not yet apply the transaction change.

00:35:44.800 --> 00:35:49.535
A completed level cannot be approved again to duplicate application.

00:35:49.655 --> 00:35:53.225
The audit records the acting officer and decision time.

00:35:54.275 --> 00:35:56.840
The final approver reviews and approves.

00:35:56.960 --> 00:36:04.255
Before applying, the system checks the original requester’s current access, target fingerprint and financial rules again.

00:36:04.375 --> 00:36:12.220
Revoked access, changed records or failed validation produce a failed outcome rather than a partial business change.

00:36:13.270 --> 00:36:17.770
The result is Approved and applied, with the full approval audit retained.

00:36:17.890 --> 00:36:20.295
The business change is applied once.

00:36:20.415 --> 00:36:25.395
This final result is different from merely completing an intermediate level.

00:36:25.515 --> 00:36:31.260
The original posting author is retained while the audit identifies the approving officers.

00:36:32.310 --> 00:36:37.915
A requester can withdraw a pending submission by choosing Cancel and recording the reason.

00:36:38.035 --> 00:36:42.595
Cancellation, like rejection, leaves business data unchanged.

00:36:42.715 --> 00:36:49.955
Use a new validated submission when the corrected change is ready; do not rewrite the permanent request history.

00:36:51.005 --> 00:36:59.265
An administrator may approve all remaining levels or decide at any level, including their own requests, but must give a reason.

00:36:59.385 --> 00:37:04.810
This is an exceptional accountable action, not an ordinary approver shortcut.

00:37:04.930 --> 00:37:08.940
The audit retains the override status, reason and outcome.

00:37:09.990 --> 00:37:14.150
Open Approvals to filter statuses and review the permanent audit.

00:37:14.270 --> 00:37:20.655
If final application fails, inspect current records and permissions and submit a new request.

00:37:20.775 --> 00:37:25.200
A deadline or reminder never automatically approves a change.

00:37:25.320 --> 00:37:29.650
Advanced administration does not bypass covered edit approval.

00:37:30.700 --> 00:37:36.355
Open a lager’s Activity link to see saved member and child activity in one place.

00:37:36.475 --> 00:37:40.365
Summaries use the established financial balance rules.

00:37:40.485 --> 00:37:43.035
Loan obligations remain separate.

00:37:43.155 --> 00:37:50.535
Interest snapshots and withdrawal requests do not add another amount on top of their actual posted ledger entries.

00:37:51.585 --> 00:37:55.865
Filter by member, activity type and date range.

00:37:55.985 --> 00:38:03.930
Activity-type filtering changes the records table, while summaries cover permitted modules for the selected members.

00:38:04.050 --> 00:38:07.220
The report follows each member’s current lager.

00:38:07.340 --> 00:38:11.550
Use permanent ledgers for historical office reporting.

00:38:12.600 --> 00:38:18.845
Export C S V includes all matching authorized activity, not just the displayed page.

00:38:18.965 --> 00:38:24.040
Lagers View is required, plus each financial section’s own View permission.

00:38:24.160 --> 00:38:30.210
A user with only Lager access must not receive hidden member or financial data through this report.

00:38:31.260 --> 00:38:36.875
Use Member balances and statements to investigate totals by member and payment type.

00:38:36.995 --> 00:38:41.910
Choose an explicit as-of date and preserve filters when following statement links.

00:38:42.030 --> 00:38:50.465
A monthly plan is not a deposit, carried snapshots are not extra transactions, and child savings stays independent.

00:38:51.515 --> 00:38:56.465
This deliberately invalid example puts positive money on both debit and credit.

00:38:56.585 --> 00:38:58.240
The form rejects it.

00:38:58.360 --> 00:39:02.555
Read the field or form message, correct the cause and review again.

00:39:02.675 --> 00:39:08.200
Do not repeatedly submit a failing form or invent values to get past validation.

00:39:09.250 --> 00:39:12.025
Delete first opens a confirmation.

00:39:12.145 --> 00:39:18.035
A confirmed deletion requires the correct action permission and a P O S T submission.

00:39:18.155 --> 00:39:25.390
Members, masters or financial records linked to permanent or protected history cannot be freely deleted.

00:39:25.510 --> 00:39:29.065
Inactivate eligible records when history must remain.

00:39:29.185 --> 00:39:31.905
We will cancel this demonstration.

00:39:32.955 --> 00:39:37.615
Advanced Django administration is reserved for active superusers.

00:39:37.735 --> 00:39:42.255
It exposes technical model administration and account controls.

00:39:42.375 --> 00:39:47.040
Ordinary staff cannot use it to bypass district restrictions.

00:39:47.160 --> 00:39:55.025
Financial histories are read-only where required, and covered edits cannot bypass the configured approval workflow.

00:39:56.075 --> 00:40:05.220
The advanced administration password-change page lets an administrator change their own password using the current password and a matching new pair.

00:40:05.340 --> 00:40:08.645
Use your organization’s password policy.

00:40:08.765 --> 00:40:12.225
Reset other users through the authorized account editor.

00:40:12.345 --> 00:40:16.020
No real password is being changed in this training.

00:40:17.070 --> 00:40:24.295
Sessions normally expire after fifteen minutes without genuine activity, unless configured otherwise.

00:40:24.415 --> 00:40:29.115
Activity in another tab counts, and the browser coordinates logout.

00:40:29.235 --> 00:40:32.805
Save work before leaving and use Sign out when finished.

00:40:32.925 --> 00:40:37.275
Closing one tab does not necessarily sign out the other tabs.

00:40:38.325 --> 00:40:42.630
You have now seen administration and every operational module.

00:40:42.750 --> 00:40:46.460
Revisit the chapter index for a specific task.

00:40:46.580 --> 00:40:59.055
Use your assigned account, verify member and account references, respect approval and history protections, and ask the responsible administrator or finance officer when an action is blocked.

00:40:59.175 --> 00:41:01.620
Thank you for completing the training.
